[agent] How it was determined, all platform-side:
[agent] - Direct SDK writes/reads from this machine couldn't reach the cluster's internal services (HDFS delta writes and Arrow Flight need direct connections that only the HTTPS proxy path allows), so I uploaded the CSV to the project's `Resources` dataset and ran the whole investigation as a Hopsworks **Python job** (`drift_investigation`) inside the cluster.
[agent] - The job ingested the 13,500 rows into feature group `drift_features` (v1, event-time `event_time`, statistics enabled with histograms), read the data back through the Hopsworks Feature Query Service, and ran a change-point scan over per-day mean and standard deviation for each of f1–f6 (standardized before/after mean-shift statistic at every candidate split date).
[agent] - The result is unambiguous: f1's daily mean sits at ~2.95 through 2026-02-26, then jumps to ~5.75 from 2026-02-27 onward (change-point score ≈ 44; day-level std unchanged at ~0.7, so it's a pure mean shift). No other feature/statistic came close.
[agent] Two platform quirks worth noting: the feature group's `compute_statistics()` helper job failed on the cluster (non-fatal — the drift analysis didn't depend on it), and the first Arrow Flight read attempt hit a transient "Set changed size during iteration" server error that succeeded on retry.
